  "prefLabel": "Mec 101.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 101.01 Purpose. The board's administrative rules set forth the organization of the mechanical licensing board, describe the board’s practices and procedures, establish the licensing qualifications of fuel gas fitters and gas fitting trainees, master plumbers, journeyman plumbers, apprentice plumbers, and oil heating technicians, establish requirements for the issuance of fuel gas fitting and plumbers’ licenses and certifications for oil heating technicians set forth continuing education requirements for the renewal of licenses and certifications, establish ethical standards for the professions governed by the board, and otherwise implement the provisions of RSA 153:27 through RSA 153:31 and RSA 153:34 through RSA 153:36.\n\nSource. #10798, eff 3-18-15; (formerly Saf-Mec 101.01) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 100); #14408, eff 10-17-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec100.html"
